From e0dcc248f78b747d177a6b2d3aa4a51458a63ddd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 07:42:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: unify feed search into ONE box (removes the separate
 filter + everything-search)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaced the two separate search UIs (car-search box + 'search
everything' icon button + separate structured filter dropdown) with a
single search input that covers all of it:
- Typing filters the car grid live (debounced), now smart-parsed on
  the backend for year/condition/fuel/transmission/state/status
  keywords plus description matching — so 'camry 2019 used automatic
  lagos' works as one typed query instead of needing the filter panel.
- The same input also shows a small inline dropdown of matching
  dealers/people underneath it (debounced, calling the existing
  universal /api/v1/public/search endpoint), replacing the separate
  'search everything' icon — click straight through to a dealer or
  user's profile.

Learned from the earlier off-screen filter-dropdown bug: the new
people-dropdown uses max-width:min(480px,96vw) plus a dedicated mobile
breakpoint, so it can't repeat that failure mode.

The old filter state (fStatus, fCondition, etc.) and its constants are
left declared but unused — deliberately, to avoid a larger, riskier
removal across buildParams()/fetchCars()/the effect dependency array
in the same pass. They're inert now (nothing can set them since their
UI is gone), so this is safe, not an oversight.
